# Vetting this recipe as a connector (agent-administered design §19.14.11).
#
# Copy this file to connector.yaml beside recipe.yaml in the DEPLOYED tree
# (~/.config/vornik/configs/agent-templates/recipes/agenda/), fill the
# server's URL, who reviewed it and when, and reload: the paired phone's
# Connectors page then offers "Calendar (read)".
#
# Vornik ships no vetted server. On 2026-10-13 none was in evidence: the
# server must speak streamable HTTP and offer the read tool this recipe
# calls by exactly this name, calendar_list_events (Google's own Workspace
# server names it calendar_listEvents and runs over stdio, which a recipe
# cannot reach). Vet the server you will use: what it reads, that the tool
# is read-only, where it sends data. recipe_version must equal the
# recipe's version; a shipped upgrade demotes the connector until you vet
# it again.
title: "Calendar (read)"
servers:
  calendar: {url: ""}
vetted: {by: "", at: "", recipe_version: 1}
